CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: insight
SCALE_REALISM: Does not hold as a positive systems claim. Evidence is L0 synthetic, lexical/hashed bag-cosine only, K<=12, no real BFCL/ToolBench/Gorilla labels, no real embedding schema geometry, and no measured production tool-choice logprobs. Reproducibility is adequate for L0 because PRE_REGISTRATION.md, run_exp.py, boot.py, cells.csv, bootstrap.csv, and logs are present, but the artifact is not a realistic-scale systems artifact.
RATIONALE: Prompt version v001. The exact claimed mechanism was not found as a shipping OSS system, but adjacent shipped/research systems already cover tool retrieval/tool calling at scale: LlamaIndex indexes arbitrary Tool objects with VectorStoreIndex and retrieves tools during query time; ToolBench reports 16,464 RapidAPI APIs and an API retriever; Gorilla reports APIBench/BFCL and retrieval-augmented API invocation. Against that backdrop, the packet’s own results kill the positive claim: schema AUC is ~0.48-0.56, at or below chance for K>=6; schema loses to generic difficulty in all 12 cells with CI<0; schema adds <=0 delta-AUC beyond self-logprob in 11/12 cells and strictly hurts in 7/12. This is a clean negative characterization, not a deployable systems design or mechanism.
